%description:

Tcp.stopOperationExtraTime:negative-alias -- a negative value ends the stop of TCP at once, as zero does.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "Extra time after lifecycle stop operation finished".

The classes: zero (0s, the default: the stage of TCP ends at once, after the other events of
the same time) and other (a positive time: the stage ends the value later; the network layer
and the layers under it stay up until then). The code: OperationalMixin::
startActiveOperationExtraTimeOrFinish() schedules the end of the stage the value later, and
sets the state of TCP to down at once. The class negative-alias: OperationalMixin::startActiveOperationExtraTimeOrFinish() ends the
stage at once for a negative value, without a timer, so a negative value is another spelling of
"no extra time". The default of the 28 other modules of INET with this parameter is -1s, so a
line such as **.stopOperationExtraTime = -1s also reaches TCP. This test fails: TCP calls
delayActiveOperationFinish() before, so the stage invokes the done callback of the lifecycle
controller inside handleOperationStage(), and the run stops with "Usage error: callback may only
be invoked if (and after) you returned 'false' from initiateStateChange()" (finding PF-9).

Host under test: host1; host1 has no application. host2 sends a ping to host1 every 50 ms from 0.525 s on, so the
ping n leaves at 0.525 s + n * 50 ms. The tester stops host1 at 1.0 s with the lifecycle
operation of INET (stopNode). The stages of the stop go from the applications down: the
network layer of host1 goes down, and stops to answer pings, when the stage of TCP ends. Observation: level 1, the last reply that host2 gets is the reply to
the ping 9 (0.975 s): the stage of TCP ends at 1 s.

%# parameter: Tcp.stopOperationExtraTime
%# class: negative-alias
%# value: -1s
%# key: *.host1.tcp.stopOperationExtraTime
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpStopOperationExtraTimeNegativeAlias")
        .once(on("host2.app[0]").signal("pingRxSeq")
                  .filterValue(9)
                  .describe("the reply to the ping 9, sent at 0.975 s")
                  .within(1.0))
        .act(action().at(1.0).stopNode("host1").describe("stop host1"))
        .never(on("host2.app[0]").signal("pingRxSeq")
                   .filterValueAtLeast(10)
                   .describe("a reply after the end of the stage of TCP")
                   .within(3.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpStopOperationExtraTimeNegativeAlias compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.stopOperationExtraTime = -1s    # the parameter under test
*.host1.numApps = 0
*.host2.numApps = 1
*.host2.app[0].typename = "PingApp"
*.host2.app[0].destAddr = "host1"
*.host2.app[0].startTime = 0.525s
*.host2.app[0].sendInterval = 0.05s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpStopOperationExtraTimeNegativeAlias: PASS
